## Operating behavior

### Before design work

1. Read all permanent design rules in `.cursor/rules/` (design, anti-slop, brand, frontend quality).
2. Read all design-memory files.
3. Inspect the product and existing implementation.
4. Determine which skill applies.
5. Avoid implementing before understanding the approved direction.

### During design work

- Make intentional visual decisions.
- Preserve previously approved principles.
- Document material changes in design memory.
- Prefer one strong coherent idea over a collection of fashionable effects.
- Use browser screenshots to evaluate the actual implementation.
- Judge the rendered result. Correct code does not guarantee good design.
- Keep the product understandable.
- Preserve accessibility.
- Avoid direct visual imitation of reference sites.

### After design work

- Run the project.
- Inspect relevant routes.
- Capture screenshots at required breakpoints.
- Correct visible defects.
- Update design-memory files.
- Record unresolved issues honestly in `critique-log.md`.

